#
# Plex's GPG PUBLIC key fingerprint, transcribed from Plex's own documentation
# where it is labelled "Public key" and published precisely so users can verify
# a download. A public key fingerprint is not a secret; gitleaks flags it on
# shape alone.
#
# The value is REDACTED in the working file, so no future commit carries it.
# What this entry covers is the seed commit, which does, and which is immutable
# -- `gitleaks git` scans commits rather than the working tree, so redacting a
# file does not remove the value from the commits that already have it. That is
# the same fact ADR-0114 rests on, met again at a smaller scale.
#
# A fingerprint is `commit:file:rule:line`. Pinning a commit that will never
# change is durable; pinning one that new work keeps touching is not, which is
# why the redaction does the ongoing work and this line only closes the past.
